    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "da3cc646-cb10-58c3-9aec-b65c6047b133",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/baseline-samples/17592186054676/assets/f3e349c521456a793fc71c2585ebfd8c13294bb07d842a752038e88383c5a69e.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-3x+3$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,6)$, $B(1,0)$, $C(2,-3)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,6)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+3 \\\\ (6) &= -3(0)+3 \\\\ 6 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+3 \\\\ (0) &= -3(1)+3 \\\\ 0 &= 0 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+3 \\\\ (-3) &= -3(2)+3 \\\\ -3 &= -3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ does not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "87a064d4-9ec9-5f27-ae10-c7d3c2726156",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
