      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/baseline-samples/17592186054676/assets/61dd9db8b33cc1ea14d69c35a22ff3f9e578ac4133d9d734d9919ad89be6b71b.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x+3$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,3)$, $B(2,1)$, $C(-1,5)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (3) &= -2(0)+3 \\\\ 3 &= 3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (1) &= -2(2)+3 \\\\ 1 &= -1 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-1,5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (5) &= -2(-1)+3 \\\\ 5 &= 5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ does not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "745b8270-926b-527c-a46c-821012a7a52e",
